<title>MEXICO: Mexico's Pemex details selected operating stats.</title>
<headline>Mexico's Pemex details selected operating stats.</headline>
<dateline>MEXICO CITY 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mexico's oil and gas monopoly Petroleos Mexicanos (Pemex) reported Thursday selected operating statistics. Figures, where not stated, are in thousands of barrels per day.</p>
<p>    Item	     Third quarter 1995	 Third quarter 1996</p>
<p>Output</p>
<p>    Total Liquids	    3,182			 3,225</p>
<p>    Crude Oil		  2,717			 2,855</p>
<p>    Condensates		  465			   370</p>
<p>    Natural Gas (Mln CFD)  3,879			 4,038</p>
<p>    Oil Products	     1,477			 1,506</p>
<p>    Chemicals		  3,443			 3,065</p>
<p>Domestic Sales</p>
<p>    Oil products, natgas   1,584			 1,708</p>
<p>    LPG			    242			   248</p>
<p>    Gasoline		     463			   474</p>
<p>    Jet Fuel			42			    45</p>
<p>    Diesel			 216			   237</p>
<p>Industrial Fuels</p>
<p>	Fuel Oil		   363			   426</p>
<p>	Natural Gas*	     228			   242</p>
<p>	Gas Oil			5			     5</p>
<p>    Others			  25			    30</p>
<p>   Chemicals (000s Tonnes) 1,604			 1,594</p>
<p>International Trade</p>
<p>    Crude Oil Exports	1,452			 1,533</p>
<p>    Oil Products		 -36			  -135</p>
<p>	  Exports		   94			    57</p>
<p>	  Imports		  130			   192</p>
<p>Net Natgas Exports</p>
<p>    (Millions CFDs)	    -69			  -136</p>
<p>Net Chemical Exports</p>
<p>    (000s Tonnes)		658			   506</p>
<p>Legend: * is the fuel oil equivalent.</p>
<p>--Timna Tanners, Mexico City newsroom +525 7289530.</p>
